when they have the same values in the same order, the same storage type and the same names?","options":["`all(a == b)`","`a == b`","`any(a == b)`","`identical(a, b)`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"49848e414b7a3da762e18afe","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a non-empty logical vector `cond` without missing values, which expression always gives the same result as `all(cond)`?","options":["`sum(cond) == length(cond)`","`sum(cond) > 0`","`mean(cond) > 0.5`","`sum(!cond) == length(cond)`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a3bfecfa0fb9284157cfe75e","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R print for `sum(c(3, 8, 5, 9, 6) > 5)`?","options":["`[1] 4`","`[1] 23`","`[1] 5`","`[1] 3`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1ab983108de7e585950f5a68","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(12, 7, 15, 3)`, what does R print for `mean(x >= 7)`?","options":["`[1] 11.33333`","`[1] 0.75`","`[1] 3`","`[1] 0.5`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b502da5fd30de5e8b2016936","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(4, 9, 2)`, what does R print for `c(any(x > 8), all(x > 3))`?","options":["`[1] FALSE  TRUE`","`[1] TRUE TRUE`","`[1]  TRUE FALSE`","`[1] 1 2`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"140d3a280df1c52b1013b512","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For `cond <- c(4, NA, 9, 7) > 5`, what does R print for `c(sum(cond), sum(cond, na.rm = TRUE))`?","options":["`[1] NA  2`","`[1] 2 2`","`[1] NA NA`","`[1] NA  3`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7d71a9a994453c23f3bcddd3","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(1, 3, 5, 7, 4)`, what does R print for `sum(x > 2 & x < 6)`?","options":["`[1] 5`","`[1] 12`","`[1] 8`","`[1] 3`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5bdc0b970f5b8eec0a4ec680","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(4, 9, 2, 9)`, what does R print for `sum(x == max(x))`?","options":["`[1] 9`","`[1] 2`","`[1] 18`","`[1] 1`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c75bf42881be2f5057a86a43","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Vectors `pay` and `sex` hold the monthly pay and the sex (`\"F\"` or `\"M\"`) of the same workers, without missing values. Which expression gives the share of the female workers who earn more than 3000?","options":["`mean(sex == \"F\" & pay > 3000)`","`sum(sex == \"F\" & pay > 3000) / sum(pay > 3000)`","`mean(pay[sex == \"F\"] > 3000)`","`mean(pay > 3000)`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d8f55c67c6db1af929515503","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For which logical vector `cond` do `any(cond)` and `sum(cond) > 0` give different results?","options":["`c(NA, FALSE, TRUE)`","`c(FALSE, NA)`","`c(FALSE, FALSE)`","`logical(0)`, the empty logical vector"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5d1d3524048b2e15adec396d","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What does R print for `mean(c(TRUE, NA, FALSE, TRUE), na.rm = TRUE)`?","options":["`[1] 0.5`","`[1] 0.75`","`[1] NA`","`[1] 0.6666667`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a57f78aabf548b224d03527e","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"A four-question quiz has the answer key `key <- c(\"b\", \"a\", \"a\", \"c\")`, and a student answered `answers <- c(\"b\", \"c\", \"a\", \"d\")`. What does `sum(answers == key)` return?","options":["`[1] 3`","`[1] 2`","`[1] 0.5`","`[1] 4`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a94438f59ac5e0421861881e","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For `v <- c(FALSE, NA, FALSE)`, what does R print for `c(any(v), all(v))`?","options":["`[1] FALSE FALSE`","`[1] NA NA`","`[1]    NA FALSE`","`[1] FALSE    NA`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5bd8d98541829c3745a9106f","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For the matrix `m <- matrix(c(1, 6, 3, 8), nrow = 2)`, what does R print for `sum(m > 4)`?","options":["`[1] 2`","`[1] 14`","`[1] 1 1`","`[1] 4`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8604d84795746b7bfaf46f83","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a numeric vector `x` without missing values, which expression is `TRUE` exactly when no element of `x` is negative?","options":["`any(!(x < 0))`","`!all(x < 0)`","`all(x > 0)`","`!any(x < 0)`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fce3e064b83ed6e27f42dd11","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For `prices <- c(250, 800, 40)`, the check `all(prices[prices > 1000] > 0)` returns `TRUE`, although no price exceeds 1000. Why?","options":["When no price matches, `prices[prices > 1000]` keeps all three prices, and they are positive.","`all()` of an empty vector is `TRUE`, because no element fails the test.","The empty selection becomes `NA`, and `all()` skips missing values.","`all()` is `TRUE` as soon as one of the prices is positive."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"479832e504e45fdc155882e6","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(1, 2, 1, 2)` and `y <- c(1, 2)`, what does R print for `c(all(x == y), identical(x, y))`?","options":["`[1]  TRUE FALSE`","`[1] FALSE FALSE`","`[1]  TRUE FALSE`, after the warning `longer object length is not a multiple of shorter object length`","`[1] TRUE TRUE`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fff4a1d142222685dd7a7a45","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_counting_with_logical_vectors_a851b89f_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For `x <- c(a = 1, b = 2)`, what does R return for `identical(x, c(1, 2))`, and why?","options":["`TRUE`, because both hold the values 1 and 2 in the same order","`FALSE`, because one vector is stored as integer and the other as double","`FALSE`, because `x` carries the names `a` and `b` and the other vector has none","`TRUE TRUE`, one answer for each pair of elements"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"80e30ef2ec2d181bfabf03f5","time_limit":40}]}}